Well, first congratulations on getting this healer up and running. You 
have successfully done what I have been thus far unable to do, which is 
get a healer up to a respectable level.

That being said, there is still a lot of work to do to get up to a point 
where you are ready to face Rodney, steal the amulet and make a 
successful ascension run.

Magic resistance is going to be a priority. I would absolutely choose 
the GDSM over a ring of slow digestion if you have a wish. I wouldn't 
think twice about that unless I was going for a foodless ascension. 
Since this is your first ascension, don't worry about conducts, worry 
about survival. GDSM is the ticket. It also doesn't interfere with 
spellcasting and will confer magic resistance.

Alternately, if you have a last wish, you might consider a blessed 
figurine of an Archon. They still make the best pets, and you can give 
it your vorpal blade while wielding frostbrand.

I would prefer the robe over the cloak of displacement. Displacement 
cloaks don't confer cancellation resistance and also don't fool the 
sorts of monsters you'll face later. They are great in the 
early/middlegame but not later.

Yes, before descending into gehennom make sure all your gear is 
fooproofed and make sure you aren't keeping potions or scrolls that you 
need in your main inventory. Dump garbage you don't need and stock up on 
food.

Nice to have on an ascension run are scrolls of gold detection and some 
method of confusion, so you can find the portals easier. Nothing is 
worse than spending a couple thousand turns on the plane of air dodging 
air elementals because you can't seem to find the stupid portal.

My thoughts on crowning is this: I say being crowned very early can be a 
bad thing. However, if you need some intrinsics you haven't been able to 
pick up for whatever reason (esp. poison or sleep resistance) and you 
are about to enter Gehennon anyway, crowning is a good thing. You can't 
pray down there in any case - why not get crowned beforehand? By then 
you won't need to pray much anyway and you'll only get the chance in 
Vlad's tower and on the ascension run. No reason not to cash in.

One last note: you can never have enough methods of removing a curse in 
the end game. Wands of teleportation are your friend - you may not be 
able to teleport yourself on some levels but you can sure teleport other 
beasties (I don't recommend trying it on the riders though - they have a 
bad tendency to wind up right next to you). Also, don't panic. If 
something bad happens, stay calm. If you have to, save the game, think 
about the predicament over dinner or in the shower, and come back to the 
game later. The worst thing you can do is act precipitously in a bad 
situation.

That is my humble advice. Good luck!

